      "writtenOn": "2013-11-07T00:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your excellent suggestion of attempting to decode and catching an error is exactly how this was originally coded (please see prior submissions and review comments). During further testing I discovered the stock decoders didn\u0027t always raise an exception, instead they returned a zero length result. I could have also tested for zero length results as well as raised exceptions, but one wonders how reliable the decoders are and what corner cases they might miss, thus I concluded this was a more reliable and robust test and possibly more efficient than doing a full decode.",
