    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAATn//lQ4\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/base64utils.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 313,
      "author": {
        "id": 8116
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-11-07T00:26:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The idea is not to require a user of the module from having to know specific escaping rules and which Python function provides the matching semantics and where to find it. Also these functions do some extra validation to catch any mangled text helping to assure the text is valid. I just noticed the decode function omitted the validation and the next submission fixes that omission. It\u0027s also appropriate to have the API be symmetric offering both encode and decode operations.\n\nFWIW urllib.unquote() is actually overkill if one follows the rules because of the constrained set of characters in base64url context, so these functions could have implemented differently.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAATn//sL8\u003d",
      "revId": "1f872abb80c262e10730d86d1ef068bda0dea989",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
